France's Minister of Justice, Gérald Darmanin has hailed Algerian security services for their work in the arrest of an alleged key figure in Marseille's crime world.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b9eb3a88-60e4-11f1-820c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-05T072936Z-1032450962-RC2B0IAD7AAM-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-CRIME.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b9eb3a88-60e4-11f1-820c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-05T072936Z-1032450962-RC2B0IAD7AAM-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-CRIME.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5dee52f6-90b9-11f1-af78-290a92cb9c17</guid><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 12:14:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b9eb3a88-60e4-11f1-820c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-05T072936Z-1032450962-RC2B0IAD7AAM-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-CRIME.jpg">REUTERS - Manon Cruz</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French wildfires expose cache of buried Second World War shells</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260803-french-wildfires-expose-buried-wwii-shells-gironde-bordeaux</link><description>
Devastating wildfires in the southwest of France have uncovered a hidden cache of Second World War-era shells in the village of Le Porge, adding an explosive edge to an already dangerous situation. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/03b403a0-8f31-11f1-a3ef-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3U66TE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/03b403a0-8f31-11f1-a3ef-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3U66TE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a62a351e-8f31-11f1-ad8f-35df43690abf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 15:04:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/03b403a0-8f31-11f1-a3ef-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3U66TE.jpg">© AFP - ROMAIN PERROCHEAU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French court rejects pro-Kremlin commentator's deportation appeal</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260803-french-court-rejects-pro-kremlin-commentator-s-deportation-appeal</link><description>
A Paris court on Monday rejected an appeal by a Russian television commentator against an order to leave France, after authorities accused her of spreading pro-Kremlin propaganda. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/62042cca-6031-11f1-9bbe-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/KF-Cnews-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/62042cca-6031-11f1-9bbe-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/KF-Cnews-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ad3b04d0-8f29-11f1-a683-ed1e659f4e53</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 11:09:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/62042cca-6031-11f1-9bbe-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/KF-Cnews-2.jpg">© screenshot Youtube</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Wildfire threat eases across France, despite heat alerts and storm warnings</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260803-wildfire-threat-eases-across-france-despite-heat-alerts-and-storm-warnings</link><description>
France’s wildfire situation showed signs of improvement on Monday, with thousands of residents and tourists preparing to return to evacuated areas in the south-west, even as firefighters remained on alert amid high temperatures, low humidity and a new risk of severe thunderstorms.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dc8324a8-8f14-11f1-85fb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RB2NX.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dc8324a8-8f14-11f1-85fb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RB2NX.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f5a933dc-8f0f-11f1-af09-fda0ec721e5e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 09:37:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dc8324a8-8f14-11f1-85fb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RB2NX.jpg">AFP - ROMAIN PERROCHEAU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France tightens foreign investment checks amid national security concerns</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260803-france-tightens-checks-on-foreign-investment-amid-concerns-over-national-security</link><description>
France is strengthening its oversight of non-European investment in strategically important companies, lowering the threshold at which foreign share purchases require government approval.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd3aabce-8f09-11f1-8052-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2UL24Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd3aabce-8f09-11f1-8052-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2UL24Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ad56355e-8f09-11f1-860b-fda0ec721e5e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 07:23:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd3aabce-8f09-11f1-8052-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2UL24Z.jpg">AFP - DIMITAR DILKOFF</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French public hospital deficit at third highest level in 20 years, study shows</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260731-french-public-hospital-deficit-at-third-highest-level-in-20-years-study-shows</link><description>
The deficit for French public hospitals is estimated at around €2.3 billion for 2025 – the "third-highest level" in the past twenty years – although it is down on the record high of 2024, according to a study published this week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d02c9bac-87e6-11f0-bc08-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22012537034241.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d02c9bac-87e6-11f0-bc08-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22012537034241.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e63ccc2-8bf9-11f1-929c-2390f09169c1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 31 Jul 2026 20:47:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d02c9bac-87e6-11f0-bc08-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22012537034241.jpg">© Michel Euler / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>As Bordeaux blaze eases, Ukraine sends reinforcements to France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260731-as-bordeaux-blaze-eases-ukraine-sends-reinforcements-to-france</link><description>
French Interior Minister Laurent Nunez said on Friday that 308 people have been detained nationwide over the wildfire outbreak, with two-thirds suspected of "deliberate arson". The announcement came as the blaze near Bordeaux showed signs of easing and Ukraine dispatched 70 rescuers to help battle the fires still burning across France.
